{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SilverRatioCounitExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SilverRatioCounitExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.silver_separates_target_from_control","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.silver_separates_target_from_control","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L123-L127","doc":"**The two evaluations together**, as the single statement the exclusion\ncites: at the silver ratio the target vanishes while the control does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.chiBlock3_silver_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.chiBlock3_silver_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L104-L121","doc":"**CONTROL — `chiBlock3` does NOT vanish at the silver ratio.**\n\n`chiBlock3` *is* a difference of two typed-word counits (namely\n`q¹·([2]_q/2)² − q³·([2]_q/2)²`), so if the exclusion argument also excluded it\nthe argument would be proving too much. It does not: the value here is\n`−12 − 8√2 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bracket2half_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bracket2half_silver","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**`[2]_q/2 = √2` exactly at the silver ratio.** The second evaluation the\nargument turns on: it is what makes the right-hand side of the forced\nequation a power of `√2` rather than of an arbitrary real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.epsNP_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.epsNP_silver","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L86-L92","doc":"**`epsNP` vanishes at the silver ratio.** This is what makes the exclusion\nrun: the target of the search is zero at a point where every candidate is a\nproduct of units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.chiBlock3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.chiBlock3","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The verified per-block character `χ₍₃₎(β_n − β_p)`, as a function of `q`.\nMirrors `chi_block_3`; used here only as the CONTROL. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bracket2half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bracket2half","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L78-L80","doc":"Half the quantum integer, `[2]_q/2 = (q²+1)/(2q)` — the counit of the\n`averaged` typed crossing `σ − h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.epsNP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.epsNP","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The corpus's asserted counit `ε(Δ)`, as a function of `q`:\n`epsNP q = (q²−1)(q²−2q−1)/(2q²)`.  Mirrors\n`QOU.Interactions.QBetaEnergyScale.epsNPq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.silver_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.silver_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L69-L71","doc":"`silver ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.one_lt_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.one_lt_silver","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L65-L67","doc":"`1 < silver`; used to force the exponent on the unit to vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.silver_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.silver_root","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**The silver ratio is a root of `q² − 2q − 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sq_sqrt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sq_sqrt_two","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`(√2)² = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sqrt_two_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sqrt_two_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L52-L54","doc":"`√2 > 0`, used throughout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.silver","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverRatioCounitExclusion.lean#L49-L50","doc":"The silver ratio `1 + √2`, the positive root of `q² − 2q − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}